{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeupcBwNApjZWTvPeHCNz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add a `status: OrderStatus` field to the Order data class and create an OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: \n   - Inject InMemoryShipmentRepository as a dependency\n   - Create a new `cancel(@PathVariable orderId: String)` method as a POST endpoint\n   - Logic: First check if order exists (404 if not), then check if any shipment is CONFIRMED (409 if so), then update order status to CANCELLED and cancel all CREATED shipments, return the updated order\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt**: No changes needed - can access shipments through controller injection\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add a `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for an order\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**: Modify the create endpoint to check if the order exists and is not CANCELLED; if CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with appropriate error code\n\n6. **ApiError.kt**: Add two new ErrorCode values:\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` - for when trying to create a shipment for a cancelled order\n   - `SHIPMENT_ORDER_MUST_EXIST_AND_BE_ACTIVE` or similar - for when trying to create shipment for cancelled order\n\n   Actually, looking at the requirement again: \"Once an order is CANCELLED, creating a shipment for it (`POST /shipments`) is rejected with HTTP 409. Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current behaviour.\"\n   \n   This means: if order is CANCELLED -> 409. If order doesn't exist -> keep current (which seems to allow it). Let me add: `ORDER_CANCELLED_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT`\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Cancel an active order successfully\n   - Get cancelled order shows CANCELLED status\n   - Retry cancel on already-cancelled order succeeds\n   - Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n   - Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test for rejecting shipment creation for cancelled order\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using a service layer: The current architecture doesn't have services - logic is directly in controllers. Following the existing pattern means adding logic to the controller rather than extracting to a service, which would be unrelated refactoring.\n- Adding a TransactionManager: This is an in-memory system with no need for transaction management; the all-or-nothing semantics are achieved by checking before modifying.\n- Making OrderStatus a property of the database-backed entity: Already ruled out by \"in-memory\" and \"no new dependencies\"; following existing patterns.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel flow - success (ACTIVE order)**:\n   - POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Read order from repository (404 if not found)\n   - Check if order status is ACTIVE (if CANCELLED, return 200 with order as-is)\n   - Find all shipments for this order\n   - Check if any shipment has status CONFIRMED (409 if found - no changes made)\n   - Update order status to CANCELLED\n   - Update all shipments with status CREATED to CANCELLED\n   - Return 200 with updated order\n\n2. **Cancel flow - already cancelled**:\n   - POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Read order from repository (404 if not found)\n   - Check if order status is CANCELLED (return 200 with order as-is - success)\n\n3. **Cancel flow - error with confirmed shipment**:\n   - POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Read order (404 if not found)\n   - Check if order status is ACTIVE\n   - Find all shipments\n   - If any is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException - nothing is modified\n\n4. **Create shipment flow - cancelled order**:\n   - POST /shipments\n   - Create shipment request with orderId\n   - Check if order exists and is ACTIVE (if not exist, allow; if CANCELLED, throw 409)\n   - Create shipment with CREATED status\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. Test cancelling an active order - verifies order status changes and CREATED shipments are cancelled\n2. Test cancelling an already-cancelled order - verifies success without error\n3. Test cancelling with a CONFIRMED shipment - verifies 409 and no state changes\n4. Test cancelling non-existent order - verifies 404\n5. Test cancelling order with mix of CREATED and CONFIRMED shipments - verifies 409 blocks entire operation\n6. Test creating shipment for cancelled order - verifies 409 rejection\n7. Test that existing tests still pass (order and shipment CRUD operations)\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me start implementing the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1298,"cache_read_input_tokens":19898,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1298},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8812fbe-5fff-4d24-9580-c1fff35c8d94","uuid":"d4b4d960-c9ff-48a9-be88-1ed67d13920a","timestamp":"2026-09-10T13:16:24.444Z","request_id":"req_011CeupcBCiBPiyqWw19BK8X"}
